---
/**
 * install.astro — how to install the Apelles beta on a Mac.
 *
 * What it is: the steps a beta tester follows, from the download on GitHub
 * Releases to the first launch, written against what the beta build actually
 * does (D-388 ad-hoc signing, D-389 bundled ffmpeg, D-390 the AI environment
 * built in app data, D-391 Motion left out).
 * What it does NOT do: pretend the app is notarized. It is not, and macOS says
 * so once; the page shows that exact dialog and explains why rather than
 * hiding it. The screenshot is a real capture of it, from the owner's Mac.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';

const RELEASES = 'https://github.com/theashishmaurya/ApellesStudio/releases/latest';
const ISSUES = 'https://github.com/theashishmaurya/ApellesStudio/issues';
const UNQUARANTINE = 'xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine /Applications/Apelles.app';
---

<Base
  title="Install the beta — Apelles"
  description="How to install the Apelles beta on an Apple Silicon Mac: download the DMG from GitHub, drag it to Applications, and allow it once in Privacy & Security."
>
  <PageHead
    eyebrow="Beta"
    title="Install the beta"
    lede="Five minutes, once. Apelles is free and open source; the only unusual step is telling macOS you trust an app Apple has not reviewed yet."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2>What you need</h2>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li>A Mac with Apple Silicon (M1 or later). Intel Macs are not supported.</li>
        <li>macOS 13 Ventura or later.</li>
        <li>
          About 3 GB of free space: the app itself is 250 MB, and its AI features set up about 2 GB
          more on first launch.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>1. Download</h2>
      <p>
        Open the <a class="link" href={RELEASES} rel="noopener">latest release on GitHub</a> and,
        under <strong>Assets</strong>, download the file ending in
        <code class="mono">_aarch64.dmg</code>.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Move it to Applications</h2>
      <p>
        Open the downloaded <code class="mono">.dmg</code> and drag <strong>Apelles</strong> onto the
        <strong>Applications</strong> folder beside it. Then eject the disk image.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Open it, and allow it once</h2>
      <p>Open Apelles from Applications. The first time, macOS stops it with this:</p>
      <figure class="dialog">
        <img
          src="/install/not-opened.webp"
          alt="macOS dialog: “Apelles” Not Opened. Apple could not verify “Apelles” is free of malware that may harm your Mac or compromise your privacy. Buttons: Done, Move to Bin."
          width="520"
          height="470"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </figure>
      <ol class="plain steps">
        <li>Click <strong>Done</strong>. Do not move it to the Bin.</li>
        <li>
          Open <strong>System Settings</strong> → <strong>Privacy &amp; Security</strong>, and
          scroll down to <strong>Security</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          Next to <em>“Apelles” was blocked to protect your Mac</em>, click
          <strong>Open Anyway</strong>, and confirm with your password or Touch ID.
        </li>
        <li>Click <strong>Open Anyway</strong> once more in the dialog that follows.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        From then on Apelles opens like any other app. macOS asks once per download, so a newer
        beta you download later goes through these four steps one more time.
      </p>

      <h3>Why macOS asks</h3>
      <p>
        Apple only skips this step for apps signed with a paid Apple developer certificate and
        scanned by Apple (“notarized”). The beta is signed, but not with that certificate yet, so
        macOS cannot vouch for it and leaves the decision to you. Nothing is wrong with the file;
        the full source it is built from is public on
        <a class="link" href="https://github.com/theashishmaurya/ApellesStudio" rel="noopener"
          >GitHub</a
        >, and you can build it yourself instead.
      </p>

      <h3>Or, from Terminal</h3>
      <p>
        If you are comfortable in Terminal, this clears the “downloaded from the internet” flag so
        the dialog never appears. Run it after step 2:
      </p>
      <pre class="cmd"><code class="mono">{UNQUARANTINE}</code></pre>

      <h2>4. First launch</h2>
      <p>
        Editing works straight away. In the background, Apelles sets up its AI environment
        (transcription, subject masks, depth) — about 2 GB, downloaded once. AI features become
        available as soon as it finishes, and each model downloads the first time you use its
        feature. Everything runs on your Mac; nothing you edit is uploaded.
      </p>

      <h2>What is in this beta</h2>
      <ul class="plain">
        <li><strong>Edit</strong> — the multi-track editor, transcript cuts and retakes, export.</li>
        <li><strong>Colorist</strong> — grading, AI masks, relight, scopes.</li>
        <li>
          <strong>Motion</strong> is not in the first beta. Its export needs Node.js and a headless
          Chrome; it returns once the app can download those for you on first use.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Agents.</strong> Any MCP client (Claude Code, Claude Desktop, Cursor…) can drive
          the app: the plug icon in the title bar opens <strong>Connect an agent</strong>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Something broke?</h2>
      <p>
        Please <a class="link" href={ISSUES} rel="noopener">open an issue on GitHub</a> with what
        you did and what happened. The app's log is at
        <code class="mono">~/Library/Logs/studio.apelles.app/app.log</code>; attaching it helps a
        lot.
      </p>

      <h2>Uninstall</h2>
      <p>
        Drag Apelles from Applications to the Bin. To also remove its AI environment, models and
        settings, delete
        <code class="mono">~/Library/Application Support/studio.apelles.app</code>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prose h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--pigment-basalt-soft);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .prose .link {
    color: var(--pigment-terracotta);
    border-bottom: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--pigment-terracotta) 35%, transparent);
  }
  .prose .link:hover {
    border-bottom-color: var(--pigment-terracotta);
  }

  .plain {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    color: var(--pigment-basalt-soft);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .plain li + li {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
  }

  .dialog {
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
  }
  .dialog img {
    display: block;
    width: min(100%, 22rem);
    height: auto;
  }

  .cmd {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--edge);
    border-radius: 8px;
    overflow-x: auto;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }
</style>
